{"route":"/docs/4.6/utilities/spacing/","version":"4.6","renderedVersion":"4.6","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Spacing","level":1},"lead":{"id":"page--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/blob/v4.6.2/site/content/docs/4.6/utilities/spacing.md\">View on GitHub</a>"},"blocks":[{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Bootstrap includes a wide range of shorthand responsive margin and padding utility classes to modify an element’s appearance."},{"id":"how-it-works","type":"heading","en":"How it works","level":2},{"id":"how-it-works--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Assign responsive-friendly <code>margin</code> or <code>padding</code> values to an element or a subset of its sides with shorthand classes. Includes support for individual properties, all properties, and vertical and horizontal properties. Classes are built from a default Sass map ranging from <code>.25rem</code> to <code>3rem</code>."},{"id":"notation","type":"heading","en":"Notation","level":2},{"id":"notation--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Spacing utilities that apply to all breakpoints, from <code>xs</code> to <code>xl</code>, have no breakpoint abbreviation in them. This is because those classes are applied from <code>min-width: 0</code> and up, and thus are not bound by a media query. The remaining breakpoints, however, do include a breakpoint abbreviation."},{"id":"notation--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"The classes are named using the format <code>{property}{sides}-{size}</code> for <code>xs</code> and <code>{property}{sides}-{breakpoint}-{size}</code> for <code>sm</code>, <code>md</code>, <code>lg</code>, and <code>xl</code>."},{"id":"notation--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Where <em>property</em> is one of:"},{"id":"notation--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-1","type":"item","en":"<code>m</code> - for classes that set <code>margin</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-2","type":"item","en":"<code>p</code> - for classes that set <code>padding</code>"}]}]},{"id":"notation--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"Where <em>sides</em> is one of:"},{"id":"notation--list-2","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-3","type":"item","en":"<code>t</code> - for classes that set <code>margin-top</code> or <code>padding-top</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-4","type":"item","en":"<code>b</code> - for classes that set <code>margin-bottom</code> or <code>padding-bottom</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-5","type":"item","en":"<code>l</code> - for classes that set <code>margin-left</code> or <code>padding-left</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-6","type":"item","en":"<code>r</code> - for classes that set <code>margin-right</code> or <code>padding-right</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-7","type":"item","en":"<code>x</code> - for classes that set both <code>*-left</code> and <code>*-right</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-8","type":"item","en":"<code>y</code> - for classes that set both <code>*-top</code> and <code>*-bottom</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-9","type":"item","en":"blank - for classes that set a <code>margin</code> or <code>padding</code> on all 4 sides of the element"}]}]},{"id":"notation--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"Where <em>size</em> is one of:"},{"id":"notation--list-3","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-10","type":"item","en":"<code>0</code> - for classes that eliminate the <code>margin</code> or <code>padding</code> by setting it to <code>0</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-11","type":"item","en":"<code>1</code> - (by default) for classes that set the <code>margin</code> or <code>padding</code> to <code>$spacer * .25</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-12","type":"item","en":"<code>2</code> - (by default) for classes that set the <code>margin</code> or <code>padding</code> to <code>$spacer * .5</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-13","type":"item","en":"<code>3</code> - (by default) for classes that set the <code>margin</code> or <code>padding</code> to <code>$spacer</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-14","type":"item","en":"<code>4</code> - (by default) for classes that set the <code>margin</code> or <code>padding</code> to <code>$spacer * 1.5</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-15","type":"item","en":"<code>5</code> - (by default) for classes that set the <code>margin</code> or <code>padding</code> to <code>$spacer * 3</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"notation--item-16","type":"item","en":"<code>auto</code> - for classes that set the <code>margin</code> to auto"}]}]},{"id":"notation--paragraph-6","type":"paragraph","en":"(You can add more sizes by adding entries to the <code>$spacers</code> Sass map variable.)"},{"id":"examples","type":"heading","en":"Examples","level":2},{"id":"examples--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Here are some representative examples of these classes:"},{"id":"examples--code-1","type":"code","value":".mt-0 {\n  margin-top: 0 !important;\n}\n\n.ml-1 {\n  margin-left: ($spacer * .25) !important;\n}\n\n.px-2 {\n  padding-left: ($spacer * .5) !important;\n  padding-right: ($spacer * .5) !important;\n}\n\n.p-3 {\n  padding: $spacer !important;\n}","language":"scss"},{"id":"horizontal-centering","type":"heading","en":"Horizontal centering","level":3},{"id":"horizontal-centering--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Additionally, Bootstrap also includes an <code>.mx-auto</code> class for horizontally centering fixed-width block level content—that is, content that has <code>display: block</code> and a <code>width</code> set—by setting the horizontal margins to <code>auto</code>."},{"id":"horizontal-centering--example-1","type":"demo","key":"98debb5ebeb276f3017e","height":147},{"id":"horizontal-centering--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"mx-auto\" style=\"width: 200px;\">\n  Centered element\n</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"negative-margin","type":"heading","en":"Negative margin","level":3},{"id":"negative-margin--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"In CSS, <code>margin</code> properties can utilize negative values (<code>padding</code> cannot). As of 4.2, we’ve added negative margin utilities for every non-zero integer size listed above (e.g., <code>1</code>, <code>2</code>, <code>3</code>, <code>4</code>, <code>5</code>). These utilities are ideal for customizing grid column gutters across breakpoints."},{"id":"negative-margin--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"The syntax is nearly the same as the default, positive margin utilities, but with the addition of <code>n</code> before the requested size. Here’s an example class that’s the opposite of <code>.mt-1</code>:"},{"id":"negative-margin--code-1","type":"code","value":".mt-n1 {\n  margin-top: -0.25rem !important;\n}","language":"scss"},{"id":"negative-margin--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Here’s an example of customizing the Bootstrap grid at the medium (<code>md</code>) breakpoint and above. We’ve increased the <code>.col</code> padding with <code>.px-md-5</code> and then counteracted that with <code>.mx-md-n5</code> on the parent <code>.row</code>."},{"id":"negative-margin--example-1","type":"demo","key":"de1c4fd4aad658a4d985","height":147},{"id":"negative-margin--code-2","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"row mx-md-n5\">\n  <div class=\"col px-md-5\"><div class=\"p-3 border bg-light\">Custom column padding</div></div>\n  <div class=\"col px-md-5\"><div class=\"p-3 border bg-light\">Custom column padding</div></div>\n</div>","language":"html"}],"demos":[{"key":"98debb5ebeb276f3017e","html":"\n  <div class=\"mx-auto\" style=\"width: 200px; background-color: rgba(86,61,124,.15);\">\n    Centered element\n  </div>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"de1c4fd4aad658a4d985","html":"\n<div class=\"row mx-md-n5\">\n  <div class=\"col px-md-5\"><div class=\"p-3 border bg-light\">Custom column padding</div></div>\n  <div class=\"col px-md-5\"><div class=\"p-3 border bg-light\">Custom column padding</div></div>\n</div>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""}],"nav":[{"en":"Getting started","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/getting-started/introduction/"},{"en":"Layout","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/layout/overview/"},{"en":"Content","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/content/reboot/"},{"en":"Components","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/components/alerts/"},{"en":"Utilities","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/utilities/borders/"},{"en":"Borders","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/utilities/borders/"},{"en":"Clearfix","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/utilities/clearfix/"},{"en":"Close icon","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/utilities/close-icon/"},{"en":"Colors","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/utilities/colors/"},{"en":"Display","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/utilities/display/"},{"en":"Embed","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/utilities/embed/"},{"en":"Flex","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/utilities/flex/"},{"en":"Float","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/utilities/float/"},{"en":"Image replacement","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/utilities/image-replacement/"},{"en":"Interactions","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/utilities/interactions/"},{"en":"Overflow","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/utilities/overflow/"},{"en":"Position","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/utilities/position/"},{"en":"Screen readers","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/utilities/screen-readers/"},{"en":"Shadows","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/utilities/shadows/"},{"en":"Sizing","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/utilities/sizing/"},{"en":"Spacing","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/utilities/spacing/"},{"en":"Stretched link","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/utilities/stretched-link/"},{"en":"Text","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/utilities/text/"},{"en":"Vertical align","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/utilities/vertical-align/"},{"en":"Visibility","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/utilities/visibility/"},{"en":"Extend","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/extend/approach/"},{"en":"Migration","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/migration/"},{"en":"About","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/about/overview/"},{"en":"End of Life","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/end-of-life/"}],"standalone":false,"publishedAssets":[{"url":"/docs/4.6/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css","integrity":"sha384-xOolHFLEh07PJGoPkLv1IbcEPTNtaed2xpHsD9ESMhqIYd0nLMwNLD69Npy4HI+N"},{"url":"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/jquery@3.5.1/dist/jquery.slim.min.js","integrity":"sha384-DfXdz2htPH0lsSSs5nCTpuj/zy4C+OGpamoFVy38MVBnE+IbbVYUew+OrCXaRkfj"},{"url":"/docs/4.6/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js","integrity":"sha384-Fy6S3B9q64WdZWQUiU+q4/2Lc9npb8tCaSX9FK7E8HnRr0Jz8D6OP9dO5Vg3Q9ct"}],"sourceScripts":["https://cdn.usefathom.com/script.js","https://www.google-analytics.com/analytics.js","https://cdn.carbonads.com/carbon.js?serve=CKYIKKJL&placement=getbootstrapcom&format=responsive","https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/jquery@3.5.1/dist/jquery.slim.min.js","https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js","https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/docsearch.js@2/dist/cdn/docsearch.min.js","https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/assets/js/docs.min.js"],"sourceStyles":["https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css","https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/docsearch.js@2/dist/cdn/docsearch.min.css","https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/assets/css/docs.css"]}
